-- THE HOSTILE READING. Each block demonstrates one finding of NOTES.md §4 with the surprising
-- answer asserted, so that the assertion PASSES while the instrument is as written. If a
-- later version of the terms (or of this encoding) removes the defect, the assertion fails,
-- and that is the signal. The expected values were worked out by hand from the source lines
-- cited, as everywhere else.

§ `Findings`

GIVEN h IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `A measurement`
`coma readings of` h MEANS
    LIST (`A measurement` OF `hours without response to external stimuli`, h),
         (`A measurement` OF `days after the coma at which the permanent neurological deficit is assessed`, 30)

`1 billion` MEANS 1000000000

§§ `X-1: read literally, 32.4 ends every contract at 66 Tuổi`

-- src:1379-1381 ends the contract when the insured "no longer meets the conditions to become
-- an insured under Article 1.3", and 1.3 (src:44-45) requires 1 month to 65 Tuổi and presence
-- in Vietnam. C1's term runs to 99 Tuổi (1 January 2085) and her coupon falls at 75 (2061);
-- read as continuing conditions, 32.4 would end it on 1 January 2052, when she turns 66 Tuổi,
-- or on any trip abroad.
#ASSERT `the maturity date of` `C1` EQUALS YMD 2085 1 1
#ASSERT NOT (`32.4, read literally — under` `C1` `the insured no longer meets 1.3 on` (YMD 2051 12 31) `, present in Vietnam` TRUE)
#ASSERT `32.4, read literally — under` `C1` `the insured no longer meets 1.3 on` (YMD 2052 1 1) `, present in Vietnam` TRUE
#ASSERT `32.4, read literally — under` `C1` `the insured no longer meets 1.3 on` (YMD 2030 1 1) `, present in Vietnam` FALSE

§§ `X-2: a twelve-month definition against a one-year time bar`

-- Kawasaki disease (src:3356-3358) needs coronary dilation lasting 12 months from the first
-- acute episode; loss of speech (src:3050-3051) 12 months' continuous loss. A claim must reach
-- the Company within one year of the insured event (src:1287-1289). Taking the event as the
-- diagnosis at the first episode (fork F-29b), the definition can first be met on the very
-- day the time to claim runs out: a window of one day.
#ASSERT `add months` (YMD 2027 1 10) 12 EQUALS `29.1 — the last day to claim for an insured event on` (YMD 2027 1 10) `, with days of obstacle` 0
#ASSERT NOT (`the thresholds of` `Kawasaki disease` `are met by` (LIST (`A measurement` OF `coronary artery dilation or aneurysm in mm`, 6), (`A measurement` OF `months the qualifying state has lasted`, 11)) `with the qualitative alternative` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the thresholds of` `Kawasaki disease` `are met by` (LIST (`A measurement` OF `coronary artery dilation or aneurysm in mm`, 6), (`A measurement` OF `months the qualifying state has lasted`, 12)) `with the qualitative alternative` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`29.1 — a claim for an event on` (YMD 2027 1 10) `, with days of obstacle` 0 `, submitted on` (YMD 2028 1 11) `is in time`)

§§ `X-3: two bars that block each other`

-- src:1556-1559: mild coronary artery disease is not paid when endoscopic coronary surgery
-- is claimed; src:2090-2095: the surgery is not paid when mild (or moderate) disease is
-- claimed. An insured who claims both, at any time, is paid for neither.
`both claimed` MEANS LIST `mild coronary artery disease`, `endoscopic coronary surgery`
#ASSERT `the answer on the critical illness claim` (`a claim under` `C1` `for` (`a plain diagnosis of` `mild coronary artery disease` `on` (YMD 2025 6 1) `measuring` (LIST (`A measurement` OF `number of named coronary arteries narrowed by at least 60%`, 2))) `on a sum insured of` `1 billion` `, after the payments` EMPTY `, the claims made being` `both claimed`) EQUALS `not payable` `Annex 1: barred by a claim for another condition`
#ASSERT `the answer on the critical illness claim` (`a claim under` `C1` `for` (`a plain diagnosis of` `endoscopic coronary surgery` `on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `measuring` EMPTY) `on a sum insured of` `1 billion` `, after the payments` EMPTY `, the claims made being` `both claimed`) EQUALS `not payable` `Annex 1: barred by a claim for another condition`

§§ `X-4: "the same illness" decides the late-stage amount, and is defined nowhere`

-- 13.2(a) (src:782-785) and 13.3(a) (src:816-822) deduct earlier payments "for the same
-- illness". The three lists are not aligned (35, 35 and 49 items) and nothing says which early-
-- or middle-stage condition is "the same" as a late-stage one. The same facts give 250
-- million or 1 billion depending on that one input.
GIVEN same IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A critical illness claim`
`a late-stage coma after two earlier comas, the same illness` same MEANS
    `a claim under` `C1` `for` (`a plain diagnosis of` `coma of at least 96 hours` `on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `measuring` (`coma readings of` 100)) `on a sum insured of` `1 billion`
        `, after the payments` (LIST (`a payment for` `coma of at least 48 hours` `of` 250000000 `, diagnosed` (YMD 2022 1 5) `at visit` 2 `, organ` NOTHING `, same illness` same `, approved` (YMD 2022 2 1)),
                                     (`a payment for` `coma of at least 72 continuous hours` `of` 500000000 `, diagnosed` (YMD 2024 1 5) `at visit` 3 `, organ` NOTHING `, same illness` same `, approved` (YMD 2024 2 1)))
        `, the claims made being` (LIST `coma of at least 96 hours`)
#ASSERT `the answer on the critical illness claim` (`a late-stage coma after two earlier comas, the same illness` TRUE) EQUALS `payable` `the late-stage benefit (13.3)` 250000000
#ASSERT `the answer on the critical illness claim` (`a late-stage coma after two earlier comas, the same illness` FALSE) EQUALS `payable` `the late-stage benefit (13.3)` 1000000000

§§ `X-5: the coupon can come to less than nothing`

-- 13.1(b)(i) allows four early-stage payments (25% each) and 13.2(b)(i) two middle-stage (50%
-- each), on different illnesses with no deduction: 200% of the sum insured in all. 13.5
-- (src:875-878) pays 100% of the sum insured LESS those benefits. Shown: with four early
-- payments and one middle payment made, a second middle payment is still due; and a coupon
-- on 2 billion received against 1 billion insured is not provided for.
`four early and one middle` MEANS
    LIST (`a payment for` `pacemaker insertion`   `of` 250000000 `, diagnosed` (YMD 2021 1 5) `at visit` 2 `, organ` NOTHING `, same illness` FALSE `, approved` (YMD 2021 2 1)),
         (`a payment for` `liver surgery`         `of` 250000000 `, diagnosed` (YMD 2022 1 5) `at visit` 3 `, organ` NOTHING `, same illness` FALSE `, approved` (YMD 2022 2 1)),
         (`a payment for` `minor burns`           `of` 250000000 `, diagnosed` (YMD 2023 1 5) `at visit` 4 `, organ` NOTHING `, same illness` FALSE `, approved` (YMD 2023 2 1)),
         (`a payment for` `partial deafness`      `of` 250000000 `, diagnosed` (YMD 2024 1 5) `at visit` 5 `, organ` NOTHING `, same illness` FALSE `, approved` (YMD 2024 2 1)),
         (`a payment for` `severe asthma`         `of` 500000000 `, diagnosed` (YMD 2025 1 5) `at visit` 6 `, organ` NOTHING `, same illness` FALSE `, approved` (YMD 2025 2 1))
#ASSERT `the answer on the critical illness claim` (`a claim under` `C1` `for` (`a plain diagnosis of` `carotid artery surgery` `on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `measuring` (LIST (`A measurement` OF `percentage narrowing of the carotid artery`, 85))) `on a sum insured of` `1 billion` `, after the payments` `four early and one middle` `, the claims made being` (LIST `carotid artery surgery`)) EQUALS `payable` `the middle-stage benefit (13.2)` 500000000
#ASSERT REFUSED `13.5 — the coupon, in force` TRUE `, alive` TRUE `, late stage received` FALSE `, on a sum insured of` `1 billion` `less` 2000000000 BECAUSE "13.5 does not say what follows when the early- and middle-stage benefits received exceed the sum insured"

§§ `X-6: the same shortfall lapses the contract under 26.5 and ends it under 32.7`

-- src:1206-1207: when the Debt with interest exceeds the cash value "Hợp Đồng sẽ bị mất hiệu
-- lực" (lapses, and may be reinstated within two years under Article 23); src:1386-1387: when
-- the cash value is not enough to pay the Debt "Hợp Đồng sẽ chấm dứt" (ends).
#ASSERT `26.5 — the contract lapses: debt with interest` 100000001 `against a cash value of` 100000000
#ASSERT `32 — the grounds on which` `C1` `has ended, on the facts` (`The facts Article 32 turns on` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST (YMD 2030 1 1), NOTHING) `, by` (YMD 2030 1 1) EQUALS LIST `32.7 the cash value is not enough to pay the debt`

§§ `X-7: any invasive melanoma is an early-stage melanoma`

-- src:1431: "Ung thư hắc tố xâm lấn hoặc dưới 1.5 mm bề dày theo Breslow hoặc dưới mức 3 theo
-- Clark": invasive OR thinner than 1.5 mm OR below Clark level 3. Read as written, a 4 mm,
-- Clark level 5 invasive melanoma meets the early-stage definition.
#ASSERT `the thresholds of` `early melanoma` `are met by` (LIST (`A measurement` OF `Breslow thickness in mm`, 4), (`A measurement` OF `Clark level`, 5)) `with the qualitative alternative` TRUE

§§ `X-8: under temporary cover, dying by Accident can pay less than dying by suicide`

-- src:281-298: on an accidental death the Company pays the lesser of the pending sum insured
-- and 200 million, and returns no premium; src:305-310: on a suicide it returns the premiums
-- less costs. Pending sum insured 100 million, premiums 150 million, costs 1 million.
GIVEN acc IS A MAYBE `An accident`
      sui IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A death during temporary cover`
`a temporary-cover death with` acc `, suicide` sui MEANS
    `A death during temporary cover` WITH
        `date the Company stamped receipt of the complete application and the full provisional premium` IS YMD 2026 3 1
        `date of the event leading to the death`               IS YMD 2026 3 9
        `date of death`                                        IS YMD 2026 3 10
        `date the contract was issued, or postponement or refusal was notified` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 20)
        `the accident causing it`                              IS acc
        `suicide, whether sane or insane`                      IS sui
        `a criminal act causing it`                            IS NOTHING
        `total sum insured of the main products on all pending applications` IS 100000000
        `total premiums paid on all pending applications`      IS 150000000
        `medical and underwriting costs`                       IS 1000000
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the answer on` (`a temporary-cover death with` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 3 9) `, injuring on` (YMD 2026 3 10))) `, suicide` FALSE) EQUALS `the temporary cover benefit` 100000000
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the answer on` (`a temporary-cover death with` NOTHING `, suicide` TRUE) EQUALS `a refund of the premiums paid` 149000000

§§ `X-9: an exclusion for a person the product does not have`

-- src:1032-1035 excludes the crimes of "Người Được Bảo Hiểm 2", a second insured. The
-- encoding applies it as written: a death caused by the second insured's intentional crime is
-- excluded, though nothing in the document says who that is.
#ASSERT `the answer on the death claim` (`a death claim under` `C1` `on` (YMD 2030 6 1) `by` (`The cause of a death` OF NOTHING, JUST (`A criminal act` OF `the second insured`, FALSE)) `, in force` TRUE `, sum insured` `1 billion` `, dividends` 0 `, interest` 0 `, debt` 0 `, funeral advanced` 0 `, premiums` 300000000 `, late stage decided` NOTHING `, funeral cap` NOTHING) EQUALS `the payment on a death excluded by Article 19.1` 300000000 (LIST `19.1(b) a criminal act`)

§§ `X-12: the funeral cap is the Company's to change on its website`

-- src:680-682 lets the Business Procedures adjust the cap, and src:203-206 lets the Company
-- change them at any time with effect from notice on its website. Nothing bounds it: a cap
-- set to 0 takes the funeral benefit to nothing.
#ASSERT `12.1 — the funeral benefit advanced on` (`a death claim under` `C1` `on` (YMD 2030 6 1) `by` `a natural cause` `, in force` TRUE `, sum insured` 300000000 `, dividends` 0 `, interest` 0 `, debt` 0 `, funeral advanced` 0 `, premiums` 0 `, late stage decided` NOTHING `, funeral cap` (JUST 0)) EQUALS 0

§§ `X-16: the additional benefit is "independent", and still ends with the late-stage benefit`

-- src:867-870 pays 13.4 "independently of" 13.1 to 13.3; src:1364-1365 ends the critical
-- illness benefit on approval of the late-stage benefit, and src:888-890 names 13.4 among the
-- critical illness benefits. A stillbirth after a late-stage approval is not paid (fork
-- F-31a takes 31.3 as ending 13.4 too).
#ASSERT `the answer on the critical illness claim` (`a claim under` `C1` `for` (`a diagnosis for 13.4 of` `complications of pregnancy` `in` `the insured person` `on` (YMD 2031 6 1) `measuring` EMPTY) `on a sum insured of` `1 billion` `, after the payments` (LIST (`a payment for` `stroke` `of` `1 billion` `, diagnosed` (YMD 2029 6 1) `at visit` 8 `, organ` NOTHING `, same illness` FALSE `, approved` (YMD 2030 1 1))) `, the claims made being` (LIST `complications of pregnancy`)) EQUALS `not payable` `31.3: the benefit had ended on approval of the late-stage benefit`

§§ `X-17: an accidental critical illness need not be survived`

-- src:1003-1018: "trừ trường hợp do Tai Nạn" stands before both the waiting period (a) and
-- the 30-day survival period (b). Read as written, an insured who dies two days after an
-- accidental coma is paid the early-stage benefit (fork F-18c).
#ASSERT `the answer on the critical illness claim` (`a first claim under` `C1` `for` (`a diagnosis of` `coma of at least 48 hours` `on` (YMD 2025 6 1) `, first sign` (YMD 2025 6 1) `, measured` (`coma readings of` 50) `, unable to do` EMPTY `, alternative` FALSE `, causes` EMPTY `, death` (JUST (YMD 2025 6 3)) `, accident` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2025 5 30) `, injuring on` (YMD 2025 5 30)))) `on a sum insured of` `1 billion`) EQUALS `payable` `the early-stage benefit (13.1)` 250000000

§§ `X-19: the tracheostomy bar is reached only by a late approval`

-- src:1849-1851 bars a tracheostomy already paid for under major cancer (and three other
-- late-stage conditions). But approving a late-stage benefit ends the critical illness
-- benefit altogether (src:1364-1365), so for a tracheostomy diagnosed after that approval the
-- bar is never what decides.
#ASSERT `the answer on the critical illness claim` (`a claim under` `C1` `for` (`a plain diagnosis of` `permanent or temporary tracheostomy` `on` (YMD 2031 6 1) `measuring` (LIST (`A measurement` OF `months the qualifying state has lasted`, 3))) `on a sum insured of` `1 billion` `, after the payments` (LIST (`a payment for` `major cancer` `of` `1 billion` `, diagnosed` (YMD 2029 6 1) `at visit` 8 `, organ` NOTHING `, same illness` FALSE `, approved` (YMD 2030 1 1))) `, the claims made being` (LIST `permanent or temporary tracheostomy`)) EQUALS `not payable` `31.3: the benefit had ended on approval of the late-stage benefit`

§§ `X-24: a change of occupation takes effect from the day it happened`

-- src:620-635: on a change of occupation or a stay abroad of 90 days or more, "cho dù Bên Mua
-- Bảo Hiểm có thông báo hay không", the Company may change, exclude or terminate, with effect
-- from the change itself; no time limit binds its decision. A change on 1 January 2027 found
-- after a claim in 2028 still takes effect from 1 January 2027.
#ASSERT `11.1(b) — the Company's options on` (`A change under Article 11.1(b)` OF TRUE, 0, TRUE, YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS `the Company may change the premium or sum insured, exclude benefits or terminate, from` (YMD 2027 1 1)

§§ `X-27: a late-stage condition at a middle-stage severity`

-- src:3130-3133: Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease is late-stage at a loss of 2 of the 6 activities
-- of daily living; every other late-stage activities test asks for 3 (e.g. src:2857), and 2 of
-- 6 is the middle-stage loss of independent existence (src:2221).
#ASSERT `the thresholds of` `Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease` `are met by` (LIST (`A measurement` OF `number of activities of daily living the insured cannot perform`, 2)) `with the qualitative alternative` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the thresholds of` `loss of independent existence, final stage` `are met by` (LIST (`A measurement` OF `number of activities of daily living the insured cannot perform`, 2), (`A measurement` OF `months the qualifying state has lasted`, 6)) `with the qualitative alternative` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the thresholds of` `loss of independent existence, intermediate stage` `are met by` (LIST (`A measurement` OF `number of activities of daily living the insured cannot perform`, 2), (`A measurement` OF `months the qualifying state has lasted`, 6)) `with the qualitative alternative` FALSE
